# Audit artifacts
AUDIT.md
# Negation: case-insensitive filesystems (macOS APFS default) match the rule
# above against `audit.md` too — keep the FDA-plugin audit command tracked.
!plugins/flow-architecture/commands/audit.md

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Repo-root MCP config — dev-scoped, may contain real credentials.
# Plugin .mcp.json files (plugins/*/.mcp.json) are NOT ignored — they ship with
# the plugin and must use ${ENV_VAR} substitution for any credentials.
/.mcp.json

# Behavioral test results (generated, uploaded as CI artifacts)
tests/evals/behavioral-*.json

# Local-only provisioning artifacts (certs, keys, consumer keys, etc.)
# Never committed — secrets live in Bitwarden, this is just a workspace
.local/

# Python bytecode from scripts/_lib/ linters (lint_hooks.py, lint_cadence_gates.py, …)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Node dependencies — tam-map ships package.json + lockfile; deps install locally.
**/node_modules/

# Worktree mountpoints created by /workflows:session-start (per-session, never committed).
.claude/worktrees/

# Labs TAM raw discovery/crawl intermediates — large local scratch (10s of MB per run),
# regenerable from the tam-map pipeline. Lightweight artifacts (icp.json, tam-config.json,
# manifest.json, *.csv, README.md) stay tracked; the heavy raw .jsonl pulls do not.
# Same policy applies to the brite-labs/ tree, plus its _raw/ run scratch.
docs/campaigns/labs/tam/**/*.jsonl
docs/campaigns/brite-labs/tam/**/*.jsonl
docs/campaigns/brite-labs/tam/**/_raw/

# Labs TAM run scratch — analysis scripts, run logs, heavy binaries, and underscore-
# prefixed intermediates (delete-id dumps, _seed/ inputs, scratch joins). Regenerable
# from the tam-map pipeline. Curated artifacts (icp/tam-config/manifest .json, *.csv,
# *.md) still stay tracked per the policy above — this only ignores the scratch.
docs/campaigns/labs/tam/**/*.py
docs/campaigns/labs/tam/**/*.log
docs/campaigns/labs/tam/**/*.zip
docs/campaigns/labs/tam/**/*.xlsx
docs/campaigns/labs/tam/**/_*
docs/campaigns/brite-labs/tam/**/*.py
docs/campaigns/brite-labs/tam/**/*.log
docs/campaigns/brite-labs/tam/**/*.zip
docs/campaigns/brite-labs/tam/**/*.xlsx
docs/campaigns/brite-labs/tam/**/_*

# Person-level contact exports (names/emails/mobiles) must never be tracked —
# repo is public. Company-level lists (accounts, segments) remain tracked per
# the PR #511 policy. Enriched contact rows live in the CRM / EB, not git.
docs/campaigns/**/lists/*contacts*.csv
docs/campaigns/**/*contacts-found*.csv

# Local agent config — shows up untracked in every repo; never campaign data.
/.codex/
/AGENTS.md

# Campaign audit working data — person-level contact records per the PR #511
# policy above; repo is public. The Markdown is ignored too: these are narrative
# records of identifiable people (opt-out requests, booked calls, quoted replies)
# and redacting them far enough to be publishable removes what makes them useful.
# Source of truth is EB / Salesforce / the Snowflake STG_EMAILBISON__* tables.
# Everything stays on disk as the working audit record — nothing is deleted.
docs/campaigns/audits/**/*.md
docs/campaigns/audits/**/*.csv
docs/campaigns/audits/**/*.tsv
docs/campaigns/audits/**/*.json
docs/campaigns/audits/**/*.jsonl
docs/campaigns/audits/**/*.py
docs/campaigns/audits/**/*.log
docs/campaigns/audits/**/*.txt
docs/campaigns/audits/**/*.sh
docs/campaigns/audits/**/_*
docs/campaigns/audits/**/.ruff_cache/
docs/campaigns/audits/**/__pycache__/

# Loose working files dropped at repo root — same person-level concern.
/ct_*.csv
/nora-followup-worklist.csv
/replied-never-tagged-positive.csv
/pa_proxy.json
/supp4.log

# Campaign audit working data under docs/audits/ — person-level contact records
# (names, emails, titles, reply bodies) per the PR #511 / #585 policy: this repo is
# PUBLIC and must not track them. The people in these files asked to stop being
# contacted; publishing their addresses would compound that.
# Reasoning stays tracked as markdown; the queries are tracked (they contain no PII).
# Everything stays on disk as the working audit record — nothing is deleted.
docs/audits/**/*.csv
docs/audits/**/*.tsv
docs/audits/**/*.json
docs/audits/**/*.jsonl
docs/audits/**/*.txt
docs/audits/**/*.log
docs/audits/**/_*
